Variables: 

Comment in TS: 

Use of Comment:
To explain the code
To stop executing certain portion of the code

Single line comment --> //
Multiline comment   --> /* .......... */ 

data types in TypeScript

number --> non-decimal & decimal 
string --> store multiple characters
Boolean--> true/false
any    --> any value
Enum   --> store sequence of constant values 

Steps to run your typescript code

trans compile your typescript code into javascript file(ensure to save) --> tsc nameOfTheFile.ts
2. create a html file       
<html>
<script src= "nameOfTheFile.ts">
</script>
</html>
3. Go to the folder where we created these files 
4. Open the browser file
5. Right click on the browser --> Select inspect option
6. Go to console tab ---Result or output is displayed

We have two options for storing <value>
1. Variables
2. Array
-> when we have to store single value, we prefer Variables
-> when we have to sore multiple values of similar data type, we prefer array
   



